## Context

`src/aedist/query_decomposed.py` implements RAG with per-fuel
subprompts. The name "decomposed" implies a decomposition of output,
not a RAG variant. After 0120 decides the new method name (e.g.
`rag_categorical`), this file must be renamed to match.

The `query_*.py` family should follow a single naming axis. Current
files and their actual regime:

  `query_frontier.py`   — parametric, enriched prompt, reasoning models
  `query_rag.py`        — RAG wholesale
  `query_decomposed.py` — RAG per-fuel (MISLEADING)
  `query_sourced.py`    — RAG + source columns
  `query_web.py`        — web-search augmented
  `query_multiturn.py`  — conversational
  `query_verification.py` — verification overlay
  `query_fusion.py`     — fusion pipeline

`query_frontier.py` is also slightly off-axis: it is parametric +
enriched prompt, not a "frontier" model (model selection is separate).
Evaluate whether renaming it to `query_enriched.py` or similar fits.

## Actions

1. After 0120 lands, rename `query_decomposed.py` to the name
   matching the new method value.
2. Update all imports: `harness.py`, `manager.py`, `__init__.py`,
   and any script that imports from this module.
3. Evaluate `query_frontier.py` naming; rename if clearly misleading.
4. Add a one-line docstring to each `query_*.py` stating its regime
   in plain language (no jargon).
5. Run `make test` green.

## Exit criteria

- No file named `query_decomposed.py` in `src/aedist/`.
- All imports updated; `make test` green.
- Each `query_*.py` has a one-line regime description.
- Unblocks 0125.
